            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0137" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.48N16/70: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-13T17:00:00-05:00">December 13,
                            1939—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1596. Department’s 1463, November 21. In view of the fact that buying season for
                    West African cocoa will be over within a few weeks, it is hoped that an early
                    reply to your representations will be made by the British authorities. The
                    Department understands that the Government cocoa control went into full effect
                    on December 5 but that prompt action would still enable American interests to
                    participate in the market.</p>
                <p>Please bring the seasonal element forcefully to the attention of the appropriate
                    officials and endeavor to expedite a decision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
